  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef calculus_matrix_function_gradient(X: list, A: list) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Gradient of a Matrix-Valued Function** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef calculus_matrix_function_gradient(X: list, A: list) -> list:\n    arr_A = np.array(A, dtype=float)\n    return np.round((arr_A + arr_A.T) @ np.array(X, dtype=float), 4).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
